# triary — Cursor rules

<!-- Derived from AGENTS.md (the single source of project instructions).
     Update AGENTS.md first, then bring this file in line without dropping
     Cursor-specific additions. -->

A workout-logging and scoring PWA. Read `AGENTS.md` for the full project
guide. This file is the always-on context Cursor should respect.

## Stack

- Backend: Rust 2024 + Axum 0.8 + sqlx + MySQL 8.0 (`backend/`)
- Frontend: TypeScript + SolidJS + TanStack Query + Tailwind + CSS Modules,
  PWA (`frontend/`)
- API: schema first via `openapi/openapi.yaml`
- Migrations: plain SQL via sqlx-cli (no ORM model generation)
- Frontend lint/format: Biome only
- Integration tests: Postman / Newman

## Backend layer rules (hard constraints)

- `backend/src/domain/` MUST NOT import `axum`, `axum_extra`, `sqlx`,
  `tower`, `tower_http`, `tracing`, `tracing_subscriber`, or `hyper`.
- `backend/src/application/` MUST NOT import infrastructure crates.
- Repository traits live in `application/ports/`; implementations in
  `infrastructure/repositories/`.
- `Clock`, `PasswordHasher`, and other "real-world concept" ports live in
  `domain/`.
- `sqlx::FromRow`-derived types stay in `infrastructure/`. They MUST NOT
  appear in `domain` or `application` function signatures.

## Vocabulary rules (anywhere)

- Banned structural names in any layer: `Service`, `Manager`, `Helper`,
  `Util`, `Utils`, `Processor`, `Worker`, `Engine`.
- `Handler` is permitted only inside `interfaces::http`.
- Names must pass the "verb + object responsibility in one sentence" test.

## Coding conventions

- TDD: write the failing test first. Use `proptest` / `@fast-check/vitest`
  for property-based tests where applicable.
- Validators return `Result<T, Vec<Violation>>` (collected errors).
- API errors come back as `errors[]` arrays, never `{error: {...}}`.
- HTTP status reserved for protocol concerns; domain rule violations are
  always HTTP 400 with a domain-specific `code` in the body.
- IDs at the API boundary are `{prefix}_{ulid}` strings (`usr_`, `exr_`,
  `ses_`, `blk_`, `set_`).
- `panic!` and unchecked exceptions are reserved for programmer bugs only.
- Frontend state: discriminated unions over flag soup. State lives outside
  presentational components; presentational components have no side effects.
- Function nesting <= 3, function length <= 50 lines as the default.

## Quality gates before committing

- Run language commands through `./dev` (`../dev` from `backend/` or
  `frontend/`); toolchains live only in the dev image. Do not run `cargo` /
  `pnpm` directly or install them (`AGENTS.md` "Common commands")
- Backend: `../dev cargo fmt --all -- --check`,
  `../dev cargo clippy --all-targets`, `../dev cargo nextest run`
- Frontend: `../dev pnpm run lint:ci`, `../dev pnpm run typecheck`,
  `../dev pnpm run test:run`, `../dev pnpm run arch:test`
- Full per-task-type table: `AGENTS.md` "Quality gates"

## Review gate and acceptance

- `git commit` / `git push` are stopped by the git hooks in `.githooks/`
  (`make hooks-install` once per clone) until the diff has been reviewed.
  When they stop you, have a reviewer in a separate context review the diff
  following `.agents/skills/code-review/SKILL.md` and record the round, then
  retry. If no separate context is available, treat the review as not done.
- Never bypass: no `--no-verify` / `-n`, no `core.hooksPath` changes, no
  hand-edited review ledger, no weakening of steps marked
  `# DO NOT REMOVE OR WEAKEN:`.
- Rules: `docs/review-contract.md`. Remote acceptance (ledger snapshot on the
  PR, `acceptance / verdict` status): `docs/remote-acceptance.md`.
- Decisions you cannot make go to GitHub Issues labelled `needs-decision`;
  keep working on what does not depend on them.

## Natural language

Code, comments, identifiers and commit messages are English only, even when
the issue or conversation is Japanese. Design docs in `.contexts/` and
`docs/` are Japanese.

## Commit message format

Prefix one of: `[feat]` `[fix]` `[update]` `[improve]` `[refactor]`
`[chore]` `[docs]` `[test]` `[style]`. One commit, one purpose. English only.

